**Production Storage Incident: Root Cause Analysis of Intermittent iSCSI Datastore Connectivity on VMware ESXi**

## Overview

A production application experienced intermittent I/O delays and temporary service disruption. Initial investigation on the guest Linux server 
showed no operating system, filesystem, or application-level abnormalities. However, VMware infrastructure logs revealed intermittent connectivity 
issues between the ESXi host and the shared iSCSI storage.

The incident affected the **Application-recorder** datastore, causing temporary SCSI transport timeouts, VMFS heartbeat failures, storage path 
evaluation, and increased I/O latency. VMware's Native Multipathing (NMP) automatically recovered the affected storage path, restoring normal 
datastore access without data corruption.

