## Key Learning

Application storage issues do not always originate from the guest operating system. In this incident, Linux reported no abnormalities, while VMware 
infrastructure logs identified intermittent iSCSI transport timeouts between the ESXi host and the shared storage. Understanding the VMware storage 
stack—including VMkernel logs, VMFS heartbeat mechanisms, and Native Multipathing—is essential for accurately identifying infrastructure-level 
storage incidents and distinguishing them from operating system or storage hardware failures.

